  "result": "I haven't changed any code yet. Plan mode is on, and I couldn't find an ExitPlanMode tool to submit the plan, so I'm giving it here as text. It's also saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-imperative-sunset.md`.\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py:392`), a child context is given the parent's whole `default_map`. It should get only the entry for its own name. With `{\"runserver\": {\"port\": 5000}}`, the `runserver` context looks for `port` in the top-level dict and misses. That contradicts the nested-map behaviour described in `docs/commands.md`.\n\n**Fix:** change line 392 to `default_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)`. A missing key gives the child no map, so it falls back to its own defaults.\n\n**Tests** (in `tests/test_defaults.py`):\n- A group's `context_settings` default_map sets a subcommand option, and the parameter source is `DEFAULT_MAP`.\n- The same through `runner.invoke(..., default_map=...)`.\n- Two levels of nesting, group then group then command.\n- A sibling subcommand with no entry keeps its own default.\n- A chained group.\n\n**Changelog:** add a bullet to `CHANGES.md`. The top section is 8.5.0, already released on 2026-08-24, so this will probably need a new unreleased section.\n\n**Verification:** confirm the new tests fail before the fix, then run `pytest` on the defaults, context and options test files and on the full suite.\n\nDo you want me to go ahead? Plan mode has to be lifted before I can edit anything.",
